# `3!`: the factorial suffix of a number a program declares, postfix `!` being overloadable and nothing built in
# (notes/decisions.md bang-overloadable)
'postfix operator !(n: int) := factorial(n); 24!'	620448401733239439360000
'postfix operator !(n: int) := factorial(n); 5! + 1'	121
'postfix operator !(n: int) := factorial(n); 0!'	1
